<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74182" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄντα</span></b> , τά, neut. pl.
			part. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰμί</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>(sum), the things which
				actually exist, the present,</i> opp. the past and future,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				14
			</span></i> ; butalso, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>reality, truth,</i> opp. that which is not, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				263d
			</span></i> ; <i>actual objects,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκιὰς τῶν ὄντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					532c
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰμί.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>that which one has, property, fortune</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐσία</span>), <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.102
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
